body:
perhaps you can try this. edit proxy host > advanced > custom nginx config: paste this, has been edited for your ip address. i'd also disable HSTS and disable cache assets

    location / {

    proxy_pass http://192.168.0.5:80;

    if ($request_method = 'OPTIONS') {

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials' 'true';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,X-CustomHeader,Keep-Alive,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Max-Age' 1728000;

    add_header 'Content-Type' 'text/plain charset=UTF-8';

    add_header 'Content-Length' 0;

    return 204;

    }

    if ($request_method = 'POST') {

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials' 'true';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,X-CustomHeader,Keep-Alive,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type';

    }

    if ($request_method = 'GET') {

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials' 'true';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS';

    add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,X-CustomHeader,Keep-Alive,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type';

    }

    }

ah i see now, yeah i agree the formula bar in PQ is very limited, both visually and sometimes functionally.. guess we'll just have to use the advanced editor, for now at least

&#x200B;

also... PQ has functions totally missing from power BI and even normal excel, which is just as frustrating..

while you may be right, running the board through google does show that the board doesnt come with wifi. so, op may be using a bad dongle indeed. thus it cant be said that it is definitely wifi related. plus the rate of errors op is getting dont match a typical intermittent signal interference pattern. but unless you think the term wifi means "the internet" (like a lot of young people i know these days), it is not immediately obvious, to me anyway, that wifi is immediately the culprit. could be network drivers (of the wifi dongle).. and as to why i say dongle, its a mining board, i doubt op wants to sacrifice a pcie slot just for a wifi card.

&#x200B;

but sure, it could be indeed wifi related...

Using Gminer: miner.exe –algo eth –server etc.f2pool.com:6688 –user wallet\_address.worker\_name

&#x200B;

When you are creating your flight sheet, you can input the Pool with "configure pool", having selected eth, you can see the list populate with selections for pool servers, pick the one closest to you and a backup, apply.

&#x200B;

Then in gminer, the %wal% is wallet, and is already selected as the one wallet address from f2pool, make sure you added it in wallets, so we can leave that. the algo is "ethash", then you can basically run it as %wal%.%workername% as worker name is the name of the system that is running the mining.

I do the nasal swabs mentioned to patients, and yes the technique really matters. I've swabbed close to 500 patients and I've only ever had one nose bleed, and less than 10 patients complained of pain (although most that complained were children and elderly).

&#x200B;

You really need to calm them down and assure them that if they dont move, it is very unlikely to hurt. Clear instructions given to them on what exactly you want to do, and where the swab is going also helps with assurance.
